WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.073
- All right.

00:00:01.073 --> 00:00:03.360
We have one final heartwarming
story to share this hour.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:04.560
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.160
I wanna tell you

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.980
about a game-changing school
generations in the making.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:11.813
Super cool y'all.

00:00:11.813 --> 00:00:15.448
25 years ago, a central Florida
couple was set to retire.

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:18.240
They had worked in education for decades

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.550
then they noticed how many
local kids were falling

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.020
through the cracks at school.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.790
So instead of finishing up their careers,

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.370
they doubled down bought 12 acres of land,

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.570
and built a new school

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:30.210
specifically for underserved students.

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:31.260
It's rad.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.360
Now their son has taken over as principal

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:35.850
and is continuing his parents' legacy

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:37.800
from the Caring and
Sharing Learning School.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:38.760
Let's welcome everybody.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:40.500
Principal Curtis and his wife,

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:44.580
the school's community
liaison, Tova watching on WNBW.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:45.423
What's up y'all?

00:00:47.169 --> 00:00:48.002
- Hey, Kelly.

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.320
- What an amazing family
y'all are a part of.

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:53.153
Oh my gosh.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:54.210
So tell us more, Curtis,

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.100
about your parents and their vision.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.550
- Well, my parents have been
in education for decades.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:00.799
Like you said earlier,

00:01:00.799 --> 00:01:04.456
my stepfather was the first
black tenured professor

00:01:04.456 --> 00:01:07.980
in the college education at
the University of Florida.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.890
And my mother was a
elementary school teacher

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:12.930
and when they were close to retirement,

00:01:12.930 --> 00:01:14.657
they took some of their own funds

00:01:14.657 --> 00:01:16.830
and they purchased some land

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:19.830
and took on the challenge of
starting a charter school.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.020
So they started with 31 kids.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:25.110
And in 2008, my lovely wife and I

00:01:25.110 --> 00:01:29.130
took over and we now
currently have 250 kids.

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:32.790
- Oh my gosh, that's incredible.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:35.250
So what makes this school different?

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.570
- Well, what makes us different

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:39.660
is we have high expectations for students.

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.510
We believe that every
student can be successful

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:44.280
and have big dreams.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.260
We also have high parent involvement.

00:01:46.260 --> 00:01:48.870
We make sure that our students know

00:01:48.870 --> 00:01:51.360
that they can be the best student ever,

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.920
that they can be just as smart,

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.350
if not smarter than any other kid.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:58.980
We have local community folks
that are always on campus,

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:02.310
speaking with kids about
career and life choices.

00:02:02.310 --> 00:02:03.450
And then lastly,

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:06.857
we're really really big
on college exposure.

00:02:06.857 --> 00:02:09.450
We presently have students registered

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:14.450
and enrolled at Florida A&amp;M
University, NYU and Harvard.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.050
- Also Kelly,

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:18.930
We have students that
participate in activities

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.937
that they may not be exposed to

00:02:20.937 --> 00:02:24.300
for a fraction of a
cause, if not for free,

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.490
such as the performing arts,

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:29.730
etiquette classes, and field trips.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:31.950
And for every student that
comes through our school

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:35.479
there's someone that works
here with a similar background,

00:02:35.479 --> 00:02:39.660
whether that's being raised by
a single parent, grandparent,

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:41.647
and even great grandparents.

00:02:41.647 --> 00:02:44.760
To us, this is more than just a school.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.868
This is a community project

00:02:46.868 --> 00:02:51.540
and a continuation of
Curtis's parents' legacy.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:53.370
- It's an incredible legacy.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:56.460
Thank you two so much for taking
the time to join us today.

00:02:56.460 --> 00:02:58.950
Curtis and Tova, you're
doing amazing things.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:01.560
I'm liking your post right now. Right?

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:02.393
That's...

00:03:02.393 --> 00:03:03.334
- Thank you.

00:03:03.334 --> 00:03:04.239
- Y'all look good.

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:05.072
It was a great picture.

00:03:05.072 --> 00:03:05.970
That's not all though.

00:03:05.970 --> 00:03:08.550
Our season long partner
pilot pen makers of G2

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.470
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:03:10.470 --> 00:03:13.260
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like y'all.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:14.130
So they're gonna be writing

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.080
the Caring and Sharing Learning School

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.201
a check for a thousand
dollars just to help out.

00:03:18.201 --> 00:03:20.648
(audience cheers and claps)

00:03:20.648 --> 00:03:21.870
- Thank you.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:23.340
- Thank y'all so much.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:24.300
Have a blessed day.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:26.130
And thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:28.110
Brendan Fraser, Jenny Slate,

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:30.180
Bernadette Lucas, and Lawrence Harris.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:33.023
Y'all have a great day, and if
it's not, try and change it.

